# Time zones, and the things worth knowing about them.
#
# 1. This file is in New York. Open it in the app anywhere else and the grid
#    shows `Placed` on your own clocks (14:12 in London for the first row),
#    while the entry box shows what is stored here (09:12). What you type is
#    taken in the file's zone, so a cell never shifts by being re-entered.
#    The command line shows what is stored unless you pass `--locale`.
#
# 2. It is `.convert_time_zone("Asia/Tokyo")`, not `.in(...)`: `in` is the membership
#    operator. A converted date-time prints its offset from UTC; one in the
#    file's own zone prints none.
#
# 3. In the file's own zone the clocks are taken at their word. Across zones
#    it is the instant that counts. See the Clocks sheet.
#
# 4. `now()`, `today()` and `.local()` depend on when and where the file is
#    opened, so this example leaves them out. `--now` and `--zone` pin them.

zone America/New_York

sheet Calls

Placed : Datetime

| Placed           | With  | Offset | UTC | London | Tokyo | TokyoOn | Zone | Back | Same |
| ---------------- | ----- | ------ | --- | ------ | ----- | ------- | ---- | ---- | ---- |
| 2025-03-03T09:12 | Ada   | *      | *   | *      | *     | *       | *    | *    | *    |
| 2025-07-15T16:30 | Grace | *      | *   | *      | *     | *       | *    | *    | *    |
| 2025-12-31T20:00 | Linus | *      | *   | *      | *     | *       | *    | *    | *    |

# The same instant on other clocks. New York is 5 hours behind UTC in winter
# and 4 in summer; Tokyo keeps no daylight saving.
Offset  := Placed.base_utc_offset() / 3600
UTC     := Placed.utc()
London  := Placed.convert_time_zone("Europe/London")
Tokyo   := Placed.convert_time_zone("Asia/Tokyo")
# The parts are those of the zone the value is in: Linus's call is already
# next year in Tokyo.
TokyoOn := Tokyo.date()
Zone    := Tokyo.time_zone()
# Back in the file's own zone it is an ordinary date-time again.
Back    := Tokyo.convert_time_zone("America/New_York")
# A converted value is still the same instant.
Same    := Tokyo == Placed

sheet Clocks

# Noon to noon over three nights in New York: an ordinary one, the night the
# clocks go forward, and the night they go back.
| Night   | From             | To               | Wall | Elapsed |
| ------- | ---------------- | ---------------- | ---- | ------- |
| Plain   | 2025-06-01T12:00 | 2025-06-02T12:00 | *    | *       |
| Forward | 2025-03-08T12:00 | 2025-03-09T12:00 | *    | *       |
| Back    | 2025-11-01T12:00 | 2025-11-02T12:00 | *    | *       |

# On the wall every one of them is 24 hours...
Wall    := (To - From).total_hours()
# ...but the elapsed time is not. Convert both ends to compare instants.
Elapsed := (To.utc() - From.utc()).total_hours()

# 02:30 on 9 March 2025 does not exist in New York. It is read as if the
# clocks had not gone forward, so through UTC and back it comes out as 03:30.
const Skipped = (2025-03-09 + 02:30).utc().convert_time_zone("America/New_York")
